.TH CSTRING_FIND 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_find \- find the first occurrence of a substring
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

size_t cstring_find(cstr s, const char *needle);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function looks for the first occurrence of needle in the string and
returns the zero-based index where it starts.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s        String to search
needle   Substring to find
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Zero-based index of the first occurrence
0 if needle is an empty string (matches at the start)
ccol_invalid_size ((size_t)-1) if needle is not found, or if needle is NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_rfind (3),
.BR cstring_starts_with (3),
.BR cstring_ends_with (3)
